  "issue": 521,
  "request": "Issue #521: Fix sennel flow help so parser contracts and rendered help stay consistent. Goal: make all 67 FLOW_COMMANDS leaves and flow get/set/run/report groups expose exactly the supported flags/options plus implicit -h, --help. Scope: extend the existing CommandDefinition with an authoritative option model for flags, required-value options, optional-value options, target guards, runtime options, and implicit help; project parser args and leaf/group Usage and Options from it; derive group options from child-leaf contract intersections; share subcommand sorting/alignment rendering between flow group help and help flow group; default to ascending command-name order with explicit semantic-order overrides and visible separators for long names; add registry/help contract tests and focused E2E coverage including abort, target guards, long names, ordering, resume, and prepare. Preserve command execution semantics, target guard evaluation, runtime directory behavior, and existing command-specific descriptions/examples. The issue audit found missing options in 41/67 leaves, omitted implicit help in all leaves, incorrect --agent-work-dir in get/set/report group help, long-name separator failures, and declaration-order-dependent listings.",
